332	/* ── Streaming TTS worker ─────────────────────────────────────
333	 * Speak a response aloud in a background thread so the LVGL UI stays
334	 * responsive while TTS synthesizes and plays. A single worker thread
335	 * serializes every speak (voice_channel_speak aborts any in-progress speak
336	 * on a concurrent call). The worker does NOT speak partial fragments as they
337	 * stream: it waits for the final fragment and speaks the whole reply in one
338	 * voice_channel_speak() call. This keeps a single ALSA open/close cycle and
339	 * lets voice_channel_speak() buffer the full reply for continuous playback. */

