This session is being continued from a previous conversation that ran out of context. The summary below covers the earlier portion of the conversation.

Summary:
1. Primary Request and Intent:

User is preparing a submission for the **2026 openvela AI Hardware Developer Contest** (deadline **2026-09-20**; today **2026-09-14**). Team repo: `open-vela/contest2026_086_ditiekouyegoulianmeng` (team 086, GitHub user **Rustypudding**, CLA email `dokipudding@outlook.com`). Product: **kid_buddy**, an AI children's companion (LVGL GUI + voice + multi-role RPG) on a **Gemini-S1 (Allwinner R528)** board.

Explicit requests in this session:
1. **(Carried over, previously completed)** Record two deferred items; then "先不管唤醒词，把刚刚记下来那几条先改了" — commit the v2.55/2.56 repo changes and move the clock-set from vendor `rcS.nsh` into `app/kid_buddy/kid_buddy.c`. Then, via AskUserQuestion, user answered **"推，我来点 PR"** authorizing the push to their fork.
2. **Report 1 (large serial-log paste):** "第一，唤醒词会识别成openai了之类的，你看日志就懂。第二，识别成功唤醒词的时候，屏幕上并没有文字和语音" — (a) ASR renders 「你好，openvela」as "openai"/"OpenVilla", (b) when the wake word succeeds there is no text on screen and no voice.
3. **Report 2 (second large log paste, truncated by harness at 50k chars):** "现在屏幕上有ui界面，卡在猫头鹰老师的界面，只有一句sorry, i encountered an error，屏幕是卡死的，动不了，也没有语音输出，故事一句都没讲。" — UI visible, stuck on the owl-teacher screen, only "Sorry, I encountered an error", unresponsive, no voice, no story.
4. **"我重启了一下好像就好了"** — a restart cleared the stuck state.
5. Via AskUserQuestion, answered **"没点，就是喊它"** — they did NOT touch the screen before it froze; it was pure voice interaction.

**Standing constraints (must be preserved):**
- 写得平实，**"不要AI味那么浓"** (write plainly, no AI-flavored padding).
- User previously **refused** the manifest-override-to-fork approach for compliance reasons — do not re-propose.
- **Only commit or push when the user asks.**
- VM has no GitHub token and no `gh` CLI, so PRs must be opened by the user in the browser.
- Memory rule `rebuild-before-claiming-fixed`: always rebuild + repack and bump the GUI version tag before claiming a fix is done.

2. Key Technical Concepts:
   - **MiMo ASR `language: "zh"` collapse**: `packages/ai_agent/src/voice/mimo_asr.c:49` hardcodes `MIMO_ASR_LANGUAGE "zh"`. The request body carries **no hotword list and no context/prompt** — only `model`, `messages` (with `input_audio` data URL), and `asr_options.language`. This is why the English token "openvela" collapses onto the nearest Chinese-lexicon word ("OpenAI", "OpenVilla"). A switch to `"auto"` was considered but **deliberately not made** (regression risk on short Chinese utterances; needs on-board A/B).
   - **`local_client` channel is unique to kid_buddy**: `#define CLIENT_CHANNEL "local_client"` exists ONLY in `packages/ai_agent/src/sdk/velaclaw_client_local.c:21`. Therefore any `Processing message from local_client:kid_buddy:story` in the agent log can only originate from kid_buddy's `velaclaw_ask`, which has exactly 2 call sites: `send_to_llm` (kid_buddy.c ~624) and `send_raw_to_llm` (~684).
   - **`g_reply_busy` gating**: raised by the wake handoff, `send_to_llm`, `send_raw_to_llm`, `kid_notify_cb`, `wake_speak_prompt`, and the TTS worker. Cleared only by the TTS worker after a successful speak, by the immediate-failure paths in the two senders, and by `poll_timer_cb`'s error branch. **If the clear never happens, the wake loop waits forever → board permanently deaf + silent → looks like a frozen screen → needed a reboot.**
   - **TTS worker silent-skip hazard**: `if (!final) continue;` then `if (len > spoken) { ... speak ...; g_reply_busy = 0; }` — when `len <= spoken` the busy flag is **not** cleared.
   - **Timers** (only 3): `poll_timer_cb` 200 ms, `proactive_timer_cb` 1000 ms (self-deletes after 6 ticks), `idle_story_timer_cb` `IDLE_CHECK_MS 5000` with `IDLE_STORY_MS (60*1000)`.
   - **Boot-time clock evidence**: `LVGL heartbeat #N` is logged every 50 polls (10 s); #250 at 12:00:50 and #500 at 12:01:40 prove LVGL started at 12:00:00, i.e. `seed_clock_if_unset()` did run — the log window is a fresh boot.
   - **"Sorry, I encountered an error."** = `packages/ai_agent/src/core/agent_loop.c:897`, the `dispatch_response` else-branch used when the LLM produced no text. `llm_proxy.c:60` documents that MiMo thinking mode (90-100 s) exceeds `AGENT_LLM_TIMEOUT_SEC` (60 s) and produces exactly this string; `s_thinking_disabled = 1` by default.
   - **Build/pack** (2 mandatory steps): `export PATH=/home/ubuntu/prebuilts/gcc/linux-x86_64/arm-none-eabi/bin:/home/ubuntu/prebuilts/tools/linux/x86_64:/home/ubuntu/prebuilts/tools/python/bin:/home/ubuntu/prebuilts/build-tools/linux-x86_64/bin:$PATH; make -C nuttx -j2`, then from `/home/ubuntu/vendor/allwinnertech/lichee`: `./tools/scripts/pack_img.sh -c sun8iw20p1 -p rtos -b r528s3-gemini-s1 -o nuttx -d uart0 -s none -m normal -w none -v none -i none -t "$PWD" -f r528s3/gemini-s1_nand -g r528s3/gemini-s1_nand`.
   - **Serial console drops lines under load**: the user's paste contained a visibly garbled/interleaved line (`kid_buddy:story[26/09/10 12:01:54]...`) and was truncated at 50k chars; ~100 `Dispatching`/`llm_cb` lines per reply flood the console.

3. Files and Code Sections:

   - **`/home/ubuntu/contest2026_086_ditiekouyegoulianmeng/app/kid_buddy/kid_buddy.c`** — the main file being edited.

     **v2.57 edits (already built, packed, installed):**

     `WAKE_ALIASES` (now lines 93-96):
     ```c
      * The "wake: heard ..." log line prints the raw transcript. If MiMo comes back
      * with a wording the list does not cover, add it here.
      *
      * The openai/openvilla entries come from real transcripts. The ASR request is
      * tagged language "zh" (see MIMO_ASR_LANGUAGE), so an English word that is not
      * in its Chinese lexicon gets folded onto the nearest one it does know:
      * "openvela" comes back as "OpenAI"/"openai" or "OpenVilla". Both still carry
      * the 你好 prefix, which is what keeps them from firing by accident. */
     #define WAKE_ALIASES         { "你好openvela", "helloopenvela", "哈喽openvela", \
                                    "你好欧本维拉", "你好欧朋维拉", "哈喽欧本维拉", \
                                    "你好openai", "helloopenai", "哈喽openai", \
                                    "你好openvilla", "helloopenvilla", "哈喽openvilla" }
     #define WAKE_IDLE_PROMPT     "我在呢，你想做什么？"
     ```

     New statics after `g_wake_cmd_lock`:
     ```c
     /* Wake-word-only acknowledgement ("我在呢，你想做什么？"). Same handoff as the
      * command above, for the same reason: the wake thread cannot touch LVGL, so it
      * parks the text here and the LVGL timer puts it on the chat screen. Without
      * this the buddy answered a bare wake word with speech but left the screen
      * sitting on role selection, which reads as "it didn't hear me". */
     static char     g_wake_prompt[MSG_BUF_LEN];
     static bool     g_wake_prompt_ready = false;
     ```

     `wake_speak_prompt` rewritten:
     ```c
     static void wake_speak_prompt(const char *text)
     {
         pthread_mutex_lock(&g_tts_lock);
         g_tts_epoch++;
         g_spoken_len = 0;
         g_tts_pending_ready = false;
         g_tts_pending_final = false;
         pthread_mutex_unlock(&g_tts_lock);

         g_reply_busy = 1;      /* later changed to busy_mark() */

         pthread_mutex_lock(&g_msg_lock);
         strncpy(g_wake_prompt, text, MSG_BUF_LEN - 1);
         g_wake_prompt[MSG_BUF_LEN - 1] = '\0';
         g_wake_prompt_ready = true;
         pthread_mutex_unlock(&g_msg_lock);
     }
     ```
     (its preceding comment now explains the LVGL-thread handoff and why `g_reply_busy` is raised on the wake thread, not the timer thread).

     `poll_timer_cb` — the `have_wake` branch gained a `return;`, and a new prompt block was appended:
     ```c
     if (have_wake)
       {
         send_to_llm(wake_cmd);
         return;
       }

     /* Wake-word-only acknowledgement handoff. Show it on the chat screen and
      * speak it from here; the wake thread deliberately did neither (it cannot
      * touch LVGL) beyond raising g_reply_busy. A bare wake word is also the
      * most likely first interaction of a session, so this is usually what
      * creates the chat screen in the first place. */
     char wake_prompt[MSG_BUF_LEN];
     bool have_prompt = false;

     pthread_mutex_lock(&g_msg_lock);
     if (g_wake_prompt_ready)
       {
         g_wake_prompt_ready = false;
         strncpy(wake_prompt, g_wake_prompt, MSG_BUF_LEN - 1);
         wake_prompt[MSG_BUF_LEN - 1] = '\0';
