## Summary of the fix surface

- The clock is set in exactly one place: `tool_get_time.c:88` (`settimeofday`), reached only from `parse_and_set_time` (line 42) via `fetch_time_via_proxy` (105) / `fetch_time_direct` (150). Nothing tracks whether that ever succeeded.
- The clock is force-pinned to a literal in `vela_tls.c:378-381` (`1772275200`, "forcing to 2026"), which re-stamps it on every TLS handshake while below Jan-2024.
- `/remind` (`agent_loop.c:690`) and `/note` (`agent_loop.c:641`) bypass the network sync entirely with raw `time(NULL)`.
- `/time` (`agent_loop.c:557`) and the `kw_time` NL intent (`agent_loop.c:378`) do go through the tool and would sync.
- A `bool`-returning public sync entry point belongs in `src/tools/tool_get_time.h`; no such symbol exists today.
- The single best guard insertion for `at` jobs is `tool_cron.c:116-118`; for all schedules, immediately before `cron_add_job` at `tool_cron.c:248`.

