This session is being continued from a previous conversation that ran out of context. The summary below covers the earlier portion of the conversation.

Summary:
1. **Primary Request and Intent:**

   The user is preparing a submission for the **2026 openvela AI Hardware Developer Contest** (deadline **2026-09-20**; today is **2026-09-15**). Team repo: `open-vela/contest2026_086_ditiekouyegoulianmeng` (team 086, GitHub user **Rustypudding**, CLA email `dokipudding@outlook.com`). Product: **kid_buddy**, an AI children's companion (LVGL GUI + voice + multi-role RPG + reminders + MQTT parent reporting) on a **Gemini-S1 (Allwinner R528)** board.

   Requests in this session, in order:
   1. **(answered)** "烧了以后好的。你之前说的日期不对的问题后来修了吗？以及现在还有什么没修的东西吗？我现在给板子设计了一个3D打印的盒子，还没到货，所以不能录" — Was the hardcoded-date problem fixed? What else remains unfixed? (3D-printed case not yet arrived, so the demo video can't be recorded.)
   2. **(THE key request — drove all the work)** "你不改我用MQTT设置某个精准日期时间提醒的话不就寄了吗大哥，这能不改吗" — "If you don't fix it, and I use MQTT to set a precise date-time reminder, isn't it fucked? Can this be fixed?" The user correctly identified that the wrong system clock breaks precise date/time reminders.
   3. Via AskUserQuestion, the user made two design decisions: (a) when clock sync fails → **"拒绝并告知"** (refuse the reminder and tell the parent, not "set it anyway with a warning"); (b) `vela_tls.c`'s hardcoded clock pin → **"一并改掉"** (fix it in this batch too).
   4. The user **approved the written plan** via ExitPlanMode.

   **Standing constraints (must be preserved):**
   - Write plainly, **"不要AI味那么浓"**.
   - User previously **REFUSED** the manifest-override-to-fork approach — do not re-propose.
   - **Only commit or push when the user asks.** Nothing has been committed this entire session (and none of the new v2.61 work is committed either).
   - VM has no GitHub token and no `gh` CLI → PRs must be opened by the user in the browser.
   - Memory rule `rebuild-before-claiming-fixed`: always rebuild + repack and bump the GUI version tag before claiming a fix is done.
   - Do not tell the user to choco-install or re-download mosquitto — it is already at `D:\Mosquitto`.

2. **Key Technical Concepts:**
   - **The clock bug chain**: Board has no RTC → `seed_clock_if_unset()` seeds clock to hardcoded **2026-09-10 12:00** at T+0 → `cron_service_start()` runs at `agent_main.c` BEFORE network → `context_build_system_prompt()` injects `Time: <wrong> CST` into the system prompt every turn **plus** the rule `- Current time is in the header above. Answer time questions directly.` → the LLM trusts the header instead of calling `get_current_time` → `at_epoch` computed days wrong → `parse_at_schedule`'s past-check accepts it (it's later than the seeded clock) → when the clock later corrects, `cron_process_due_jobs` fires it immediately or `cron_service_start` silently disables it as a "stale job" (syslog only).
   - **The only authoritative clock setter** is `tool_get_time`'s HTTPS `Date:` header path → `parse_and_set_time()` → `settimeofday()`.
   - **Second wrong-clock source**: `vela_tls.c:375-381` force-sets clock to `1772275200` (2026-02-28 UTC) on any TLS handshake while `time(NULL) < 1704067200` (Jan 1 2024).
   - **`tool_get_time.c:185`** gated the local fallback on `now > 1735689600` — the seed passes this, so a wrong time was returned as real.
   - **`/remind`** (`agent_loop.c:670-700`) computes `at_epoch = time(NULL) + secs` — a genuine RELATIVE delay, safe even on an untrusted clock; but line 695 discarded `cron_add`'s return value and always replied "好的".
   - **Threading**: tool execution runs **inline on the agent_loop thread** for single-tool-call turns; the outbound dispatcher is a separate single-threaded task (`outbound_dispatch_task`, `agent_main.c:346`) with no watchdog.
   - **NuttX/openvela build system**: `apps/Makefile` builds `libapps.a` by having each configured app **append** its objects; comment at `apps/Makefile:43-44` says "We first remove libapps.a before letting the other rules add objects to it". `$(SDIR)_all` targets are defined by `SDIR_template` in `/home/ubuntu/nuttx/tools/Config.mk:726`. `CONFIGURED_APPS` is constructed in `/home/ubuntu/apps/Make.defs:44` from `BUILDIRS := $(dir $(wildcard $(APPDIR)/*/Make.defs))`. Per-app `.built` marker files (44 under `apps/`) gate whether an app builds and archives.
   - **`TOPDIR` is required** for a valid `make -C /home/ubuntu/apps` invocation; running apps standalone without it fails on `apps/import/scripts/Make.defs`.
   - **Build does not track `.h` dependencies** (memory `ai-agent-stale-object-header-deps`) → editing a header requires deleting stale `.o` files, otherwise struct-size/symbol ABI mismatch.
   - **`distclean` is dangerous here** — memory `quickjs-patch-drift` records that distclean re-downloads quickjs source that conflicts with the patch tree; mitigation was `touch .patch` + keeping `/tmp/qjs-keep`. `make clean` avoids this.
   - **Machine is small**: `nproc` = **2**, RAM = **3 GB** total (1 GB used, 2 GB buff/cache). So `-j2` is the max useful parallelism; a full rebuild is slow (~1–2 hours estimated).
   - **Cron persistence file**: `AGENT_CRON_FILE = AGENT_DATA_DIR "/cron.json"` where `AGENT_DATA_DIR = CONFIG_EXAMPLES_AI_AGENT_VELA_DATA_DIR = "/data/ai_agent"` (`include/agent_config.h:172`, `/home/ubuntu/nuttx/.config:4645`). So the on-device path is **`/data/ai_agent/cron.json`**.
   - **Serial console is UART2**; board-level `ps` is available; `RAMLOG_SYSLOG` is off so `dmesg` is useless.

