This session is being continued from a previous conversation that ran out of context. The summary below covers the earlier portion of the conversation.

Summary:
1. **Primary Request and Intent:**

   The user is preparing a submission for the **2026 openvela AI Hardware Developer Contest** (deadline **2026-09-20**; today is now **2026-09-16**). Team repo: `open-vela/contest2026_086_ditiekouyegoulianmeng` (team 086, GitHub user **Rustypudding**, CLA email `dokipudding@outlook.com`). Product: **kid_buddy**, an AI children's companion (LVGL GUI + voice + multi-role RPG + reminders + MQTT parent reporting) on a **Gemini-S1 (Allwinner R528)** board.

   Two requests in this session:

   1. **(COMPLETED)** Resumed from a prior summary: finish the approved plan fixing "wrong system clock → precise datetime reminders computed wrong" (user's words: "你不改我用MQTT设置某个精准日期时间提醒的话不就寄了吗大哥，这能不改吗"). This required fixing a broken build first. **Done: v2.61 image built, packed, verified, placed in the team repo. Not yet on-board verified.**

   2. **(CURRENT, IN PLAN MODE — not yet implemented)** The user reported: after power-cycling the board, it displays and reads aloud a string like `/data/aiagent/skills//data/aiagent/skills/weather.md/data/aiagent......` — verbatim: "你现在再改一个东西，我把板子断电重启以后，板子上显示一串/data/aiagent/skills//data/aiagent/skills/weather.md/data/aiagent...... 并且把这些东西读了出来。这太糟了，他应该输出一句欢迎回来之类的语音的。能不能修一下啊"

   **User's answers to two design questions asked in plan mode:**
   - Boot greeting → **"本地固定播一句，再让 LLM 续（推荐）"** — board locally speaks a fixed welcome line (no network/LLM dependency), then the existing boot-probe LLM turn still runs for story continuation.
   - Skill list when the user asks 「有什么技能」 → **"只念技能名（推荐）"** — speak/display only skill names, not descriptions or paths.

   **Standing constraints (must be preserved):**
   - Write plainly, **"不要AI味那么浓"**.
   - User previously **REFUSED** the manifest-override-to-fork approach — do not re-propose.
   - **Only commit or push when the user asks.** Nothing has been committed this entire session.
   - VM has no GitHub token and no `gh` CLI → PRs must be opened by the user in the browser.
   - Memory rule `rebuild-before-claiming-fixed`: always rebuild + repack and bump the GUI version tag before claiming a fix is done.
   - Do not tell the user to choco-install or re-download mosquitto — it is already at `D:\Mosquitto`.
   - **Never use `distclean`** (memory `quickjs-patch-drift`: it re-downloads quickjs source that conflicts with the patch tree).
   - Never destroy `nuttx/.config` (memory `defconfig-stale-vs-live-config`).
   - **Never use `pkill` with a pattern matching my own shell** (caused the whole build breakage).

2. **Key Technical Concepts:**
   - **NuttX/openvela apps build**: `apps/Application.mk:51` has `SUFFIX ?= $(subst $(DELIM),.,$(CWD))` with `CWD = $(CURDIR)` (line 47). **Nothing in the tree passes `SUFFIX`**, so object files are legitimately named `<src>.c.<abs-path-with-dots>[_N].o` (e.g. `kid_buddy.c.home.ubuntu.contest2026_086_ditiekouyegoulianmeng.app.kid_buddy.o`). Some sources get a `_1`/`_6` collision-counter twin.
   - **`.built` markers gate archiving**: `libapps.a` is built by deleting it then having each configured app APPEND its objects (`apps/Makefile:43-44` comment). A `.built` file means "already archived, skip". `CLEANDIRS := $(dir $(wildcard $(APPDIR)/*/Makefile))` does **not** cover `vendor/allwinnertech/apps/`, so its `.built` and `.o` survive `make clean` → once `libapps.a` is deleted those apps never re-add → undefined `hello_main`/`kid_buddy_main`/etc.
   - **Registry generation**: `apps/Make.defs:89` `BUILTIN_REGISTRY ?= $(APPDIR)/builtin/registry`; `apps/Make.defs:94,102` echo `Register: $1` inside `define REGISTER`; per-app `Makefile` calls it. `apps/builtin/Makefile` has `registry/.updated:` with **no prerequisites** (created once, then always up-to-date), and `builtin_list.h: registry/.updated` concatenates all `*.bdat`. `clean_context::` deletes `$(PDATLIST)`/`$(BDATLIST)`; only `distclean` deletes `.updated`.
   - **dirlinks**: `clean_context` deletes `nuttx/arch/arm/src/chip` (a symlink to `/home/ubuntu/vendor/allwinnertech/chips/r528`), after which `make -C nuttx clean` fails at `arch/arm/src_clean` with `chip/Make.defs: No such file or directory`. `make -C nuttx context` restores it.
   - **App discovery**: `apps/Make.defs:44` `BUILDIRS := $(dir $(wildcard $(APPDIR)/*/Make.defs))` (ONE level), then `define Add_Application → include $(1)Make.defs`. `apps/vendor -> ../vendor/` and `apps/packages -> ../packages` symlinks bridge to those trees; `vendor/allwinnertech/apps/Make.defs` does `include $(APPDIR)/vendor/allwinnertech/apps/*/Make.defs`. Guards use `ifneq ($(CONFIG_X),)`.
   - **Config state**: `.config` was regenerated today 15:35 from the team repo's `board/nsh_minidisplay/defconfig` (via `CONFIG_BASE_DEFCONFIG` path change). That defconfig (553 lines) is the **correct, current, white-screen-fixed** one. `.config.good-20260913` (Sep 13 05:08) is **pre-fix / polluted** and MUST NOT be used to restore `.config`.
   - **Clock fix design (v2.61)**: `s_clock_verified` flag set only by a successful `settimeofday()` from a network `Date:` header; `agent_clock_is_verified()` / `agent_time_sync_now()` exported; boot sync task before channel start with a bounded 5s wait; prompt says UNVERIFIED and forbids computing epochs from the header; `tool_cron.c` refuses absolute `at` scheduling when unverified (`"relative": true` bypasses); `/remind` sets `relative:true` and checks `cron_add`'s return; `vela_tls.c` placeholder clock no longer implies verified; `AGENT_CRON_AT_STALE_GRACE (5*60)` drops stale one-shot jobs instead of firing them.
   - **Current bug (skills/skills-summary stack smash)**: `snprintf` returns the would-be length, so a truncation leaves `off > size`; then `(size - off)` underflows to a huge `size_t` and subsequent appends write wildly out of bounds. 11 built-in skills × ~160 bytes ≈ 1760 > `char skills_buf[1024]` → guaranteed overflow every boot.
   - Machine: 2 cores, 3 GB RAM → `-j2` is max; full rebuild ~1–2 hours.

3. **Files and Code Sections:**

   **NEW: `/home/ubuntu/packages/ai_agent/src/tools/skill_loader.c` — THE CURRENT BUG (lines 346-407, verbatim):**
   ```c
   size_t skill_loader_build_summary(char *buf, size_t size)
   {
       DIR *dir = opendir(AGENT_SKILLS_DIR);
       if (!dir) {
           syslog(LOG_WARNING, "[%s] Cannot open skills directory for enumeration: %s\n", TAG, AGENT_SKILLS_DIR);
           buf[0] = '\0';
           return 0;
       }

       size_t off = 0;
       struct dirent *ent;

       while ((ent = readdir(dir)) != NULL && off < size - 1) {
           const char *name = ent->d_name;
           size_t name_len = strlen(name);

           if (name_len < 4) continue;
           if (strcmp(name + name_len - 3, ".md") != 0) continue;
           if (name[0] == '.') continue;

           char full_path[256];
           snprintf(full_path, sizeof(full_path), "%s%s", AGENT_SKILLS_DIR, name);

           FILE *f = fopen(full_path, "r");
           if (!f) continue;

           char first_line[128];
           if (!fgets(first_line, sizeof(first_line), f)) { fclose(f); continue; }

           char title[64];
           extract_title(first_line, strlen(first_line), title, sizeof(title));

           char desc[256];
           extract_description(f, desc, sizeof(desc));
           fclose(f);

           /* Append to summary */
           off += snprintf(buf + off, size - off,
               "- **%s**: %s (read with: read_file %s)\n",
               title, desc, full_path);
       }

       closedir(dir);

       buf[off] = '\0';
       syslog(LOG_INFO, "[%s] Skills summary: %d bytes\n", TAG, (int)off);
       return off;
   }
   ```
   Line 397 returns would-be length → `off` can reach ~1760; line 404 `buf[off] = '\0'` is an OOB write.

   Same file, lines 314-344 (`extract_description`) and 292-309 (`extract_title`) are **bounded and safe** — do not change.

   Same file, lines 232-244 — the 11 built-in skills:
   ```c
   static const builtin_skill_t s_builtins[] = {
       { "weather", BUILTIN_WEATHER }, { "daily-briefing", BUILTIN_DAILY_BRIEFING },
       { "skill-creator", BUILTIN_SKILL_CREATOR }, { "system-health", BUILTIN_SYSTEM_HEALTH },
       { "reminder", BUILTIN_REMINDER }, { "note-taker", BUILTIN_NOTE_TAKER },
