2. Key Technical Concepts:

- **LVGL 9.1.0**, source at `/home/ubuntu/apps/graphics/lvgl/lvgl`.
- **FULL render mode (single buffer)**: `CONFIG_LV_NUTTX_LCD_BUFFER_COUNT=1` (`nuttx/.config:4201`) → `lv_nuttx_lcd.c:174-180` selects `LV_DISPLAY_RENDER_MODE_FULL`. **Any invalidate redraws and re-flushes the entire screen.** One frame = 320×240×2 = **153,600 bytes**, ≈ **31 ms** of pure bus time on 40 MHz SPI1. Design target 10–15 fps.
- **SPI1 competes with audio DMA** (`hal_spi.c:68-72`) — aggressive animation during TTS playback risks audio glitches.
- **Screen is 320×240** (`CONFIG_LCD_ILI9341_IFACE0_LANDSCAPE=y` swaps xres/yres). The old hardcoded `SCR_W 240 / SCR_H 320` was wrong. Resolution is now queried at runtime via `lv_display_get_horizontal_resolution()` / `_vertical_resolution()`. **This has still never been confirmed on real hardware.**
- **Mask cache is keyed on radius ALONE**: `CONFIG_LV_DRAW_SW_CIRCLE_CACHE_SIZE=4`, `lv_draw_sw_mask.c:319`; a cache miss costs two `lv_malloc()`s in `circ_calc_aa4()`. Effective radius is `min(radius, h/2)`.
- **`transform_rotation` is in TENTHS of a degree, positive = CLOCKWISE** — proved via `lv_draw_sw_transform.c:90` (`tr_dsc.angle = -draw_dsc->rotation`) and the inverse map `[c -s; s c]` at `:631`, and empirically with a magnified render.
- **`lv_arc_draw()` unconditionally draws the knob** (`get_knob_area()` + `lv_draw_rect(LV_PART_KNOB)` is its last step, no interactivity test); the default theme paints KNOB as a filled circle. Must be explicitly nulled.
- **`lv_obj_set_style_*` unconditionally calls `lv_obj_invalidate()`** — an idle face must issue zero LVGL calls.
- **Why-set-only-what-changed is mandatory**: in FULL mode, writing a property every 100 ms = 10 full-screen flushes per second forever.
- `LV_STYLE_OPA` ≠ `LV_STYLE_OPA_LAYERED`; only `opa_layered`/transforms force a temporary layer (`lv_refr.c:502-505`).
- **Rotated objects each cost a temporary layer + per-frame draw buffer** (`lv_draw.c`); budget is ≤4 (brow ×2 + bell + hand).
- **`lv_arc_set_angles(o, N, N)` draws nothing** (`start == end` early-returns) — a flat mouth needs a separate bar.
- **LV_OPA_* only steps by 10** (20/30/40/50…) — `LV_OPA_25` does not exist and fails to compile.
- **CJK font**: `CONFIG_LV_FONT_SIMSUN_16_CJK=y` and `CONFIG_LV_FONT_DEFAULT_SIMSUN_16_CJK=y`; `line_height = 19`, `base_line = 3`; declared at `lv_font.h:287` via `LV_FONT_DECLARE(lv_font_simsun_16_cjk)`. Coverage: **8132 code points, 7278 CJK chars (0x4E00–0x9FA0)**, plus full ASCII 0x20–0x7F, full-width punctuation 0xFF01+, 0x3005+ — **100% on 8 realistic conversational replies**.
- **Cross-thread rule**: LVGL objects only touchable from the LVGL thread; all signalling via plain `volatile int` 0/1 or latched level flags, read in `face_apply()`.
- **Build**: `export PATH=/home/ubuntu/prebuilts/gcc/linux-x86_64/arm-none-eabi/bin:$PATH`; `make -C /home/ubuntu/nuttx -j2`. App source is `/home/ubuntu/apps/packages/demos/contest2026_086_kid_buddy` → symlink to `/home/ubuntu/contest2026_086_ditiekouyegoulianmeng/app/kid_buddy`.
- **Pack**: from `/home/ubuntu/vendor/allwinnertech/lichee` run `./tools/scripts/pack_img.sh -c sun8iw20p1 -p rtos -b r528s3-gemini-s1 -o nuttx -d uart0 -s none -m normal -w none -v none -i none -t "$PWD" -f r528s3/gemini-s1_nand -g r528s3/gemini-s1_nand`. Output: `out/r528s3/gemini-s1_nand/rtos_nuttx_r528s3-gemini-s1_uart0_128Mnand.img`.
- **Pillow preview workflow**: render at 4× supersample, LANCZOS down, quantise to RGB565 so banding matches the panel.
- Contest submission rules: code goes in the team repo `app/`/`board/`, zero changes to the production repo, AI logs mandatory, README must be replaced, deadline 9/20.

