2. Key Technical Concepts:

- **LVGL 9.1.0**, source at `/home/ubuntu/apps/graphics/lvgl/lvgl`.
- **FULL render mode (single buffer)**: `CONFIG_LV_NUTTX_LCD_BUFFER_COUNT=1` → `lv_nuttx_lcd.c:174-180` selects `LV_DISPLAY_RENDER_MODE_FULL`. Any invalidate redraws and re-flushes the whole screen: one frame = 320×240×2 = **153,600 bytes**, ≈ **31 ms** of bus time on 40 MHz SPI1. "Only repaint the face" is not a valid optimization on this board.
- **SPI1 competes with audio DMA** (`hal_spi.c:68-72`) — aggressive animation during TTS risks audio glitches. Hence throttling.
- **`lv_obj_set_style_*` unconditionally invalidates**; `lv_obj_set_x/y/pos` early-return when unchanged. "Only write what changed" is mandatory.
- **Children are clipped to the parent's rectangle** unless the parent has `LV_OBJ_FLAG_OVERFLOW_VISIBLE` — verified in `src/core/lv_refr.c:139` (`if(lv_obj_has_flag(obj, LV_OBJ_FLAG_OVERFLOW_VISIBLE)) { obj_coords = &obj_coords_ext; } else { obj_coords = &obj->coords; }` then `_lv_area_intersect`). `clip_corner` style is off by default, so the clip is a plain rectangle, not the rounded corners.
- **`lv_obj_check_type()` is an EXACT class comparison**, so labels do NOT receive the default theme's `styles.card`; a label's content width == its object width.
- **Labels do not set `LV_OBJ_FLAG_OVERFLOW_VISIBLE`** → text taller than the object is silently clipped.
- **LVGL always wraps at `max_w`**, so `LV_LABEL_LONG_CLIP` does not disable wrapping. With an explicit object height, `lv_label_refr_text()` leaves the height alone.
- **CJK font**: `lv_font_simsun_16_cjk`, `line_height = 19`, `base_line = 3`. ASCII = 8.00 px, CJK = 16.00 px exactly. 128 codepoints below U+2000 are full-width; 10 at/above U+2000 are half-width.
- **`CONFIG_LV_DRAW_SW_SHADOW_CACHE_SIZE=0`** — never use shadows. **`CONFIG_LV_DRAW_SW_CIRCLE_CACHE_SIZE=4`**, mask cache keyed on radius alone.
- **`transform_rotation` is in TENTHS of a degree, positive = CLOCKWISE.**
- **Layout constants**: `FACE_LINE_H 19`, `FACE_TEXT_LINES 3`, `FACE_PANEL_PAD 6`, `FACE_PANEL_X 6`, `FACE_PANEL_BOT 5`, `FACE_PANEL_GAP 4`, `FACE_CELL_W 8`, `FACE_PANEL_R 8`, `FACE_TEXT_BUF 256`, `FACE_TEXT_MIN_MS 250`. Face band `g_fh = 162`, panel `6,166 278x69`, `g_text_cols = 33`. Boot log: `[kid_buddy] GUI v2.66 display 320x240` and `[kid_buddy] face UI v2.66 on 320x240 (face band 162, panel 6,166 278x69, 33 cols)`.
