e65550f18759f086d7f544edcf17d1e31223244f
杜书豪 <xiaoduss@qq.com>
Tue Aug 18 17:03:40 2026 +0800
fix: stop chunked response read at terminator block

The tls_read_response read loop only stops on EOF or content-length.
DeepSeek (like most modern APIs) responds with Transfer-Encoding:
chunked + Connection: keep-alive, so the device blocks reading until
the server closes the connection after ~60s idle timeout. That trips
the agent's 60s LLM watchdog and every ask fails with a timeout.

Add chunked_end_seen() to detect the chunked terminator
("...\r\n0\r\n\r\n", or "0\r\n\r\n" for an empty body) and break
out of the read loop when it is seen, checked at loop top and after
each read.

Verified on Gemini-S1: ask returns in ~10-20s instead of timing out.

Signed-off-by: xiaoduss <xiaoduss@users.noreply.github.com>


